  "reason": "The current best is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc. We have strong evidence that multimodal + multiprofile + avgpool is the right architecture, but we have only tested concat fusion. Config_019 changes exactly one variable (fusion: concat → weighted) while holding all other settings at their best-known values. This cleanly isolates whether a learned weighted combination of modalities can outperform simple concatenation. It is the most direct exploitation of the current best result with minimal confounding, and with 5 experiments remaining, establishing whether fusion strategy matters before exploring larger changes (image encoder, RNA encoder) ensures we build on the strongest base configuration for subsequent experiments."
